This repository contains no OM Digital Solutions / Olympus firmware. The patcher (firmware/patch.py) works on the
official firmware file that each user downloads themselves; releases/*/patch.json hold only the bytes this project writes
(its own code, hooks and pointers to that code).

Based on Caduceus (cakelesscoder/caduceus-ep7, Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 cakelesscoder), firmware patches for the
Olympus PEN E-P7: the on-camera look editor design, the BUNDLES.BIN slot layout (firmware/vendor/
caduceus-bundles-layout.json), the Caduceus Control Panel web app (webapp/, built into looklab/), to which this project adds the OM-3 mode
(webapp/src/om3.ts, om3names.ts and the OM-3 parts of main.ts, preview.ts and pack.ts), and the official-firmware
download request in patch.py.

Halation (v0.28: firmware/src/editor.s `hl_run`, firmware/halation.py, research/halation/) is our own code and numbers;
its method (a threshold-excess cell grid, a small blur, then a warm tint that fades on bright pixels) follows Caduceus
for the E-P7's halation by cakelesscoder (docs/HALATION_RED.md in their repository).

Sample photos in webapp/public/samples are public domain (CC0 1.0); see webapp/public/samples/CREDITS.md.

The Control Panel's OM-3 mode loads "OM3 Label Condensed", a renamed ASCII subset of DejaVu Sans Condensed (Bitstream
Vera licence; DejaVu changes public domain), to draw profile-name pictures; see webapp/public/fonts/FONT-LICENSE.txt.

Developer tools in tools/emulator drive om-emu (github.com/flatpanda/om-emu), which is not included and keeps its
own licence.

